{#- Figure 1 of the DP series: the Laplace mechanism on a count, live.
    Driven by the site's one privacy budget (window.eps, js/eps.js) through
    js/post.js. Server-rendered at ε = ∞ so it reads without JavaScript.
    Include in a post with:  {% include "blog/dp-live-figure.njk" %}
    (on its own line, with a blank line above and below). -#}
<figure class="dpfig" id="fig-laplace" data-dpfig data-n="1000" data-range="10" aria-labelledby="fig-laplace-cap">
  <div class="dpfig__plot">
    <svg class="dpfig__svg" viewBox="0 0 560 158" role="img" aria-labelledby="fig-laplace-desc" focusable="false">
      <desc id="fig-laplace-desc">At ε = ∞ nothing is added: every release is exactly 1,000, and the neighbouring dataset’s release is exactly 1,001.</desc>
      <g class="dpfig__grid" aria-hidden="true">
        <line x1="20" y1="150" x2="540" y2="150"/>
        <line class="t" x1="20" y1="150" x2="20" y2="155"/><line class="t" x1="150" y1="150" x2="150" y2="155"/><line class="t" x1="280" y1="150" x2="280" y2="156"/><line class="t" x1="410" y1="150" x2="410" y2="155"/><line class="t" x1="540" y1="150" x2="540" y2="155"/>
      </g>
      <line class="dpfig__truth" x1="280" y1="10" x2="280" y2="150" aria-hidden="true"/>
      <path class="dpfig__area" d="M280,150 L280,14" aria-hidden="true"/>
      <path class="dpfig__nb" d="M306,150 L306,14" aria-hidden="true"/>
      <path class="dpfig__d" d="M280,150 L280,14" aria-hidden="true"/>
      <g class="dpfig__rel" aria-hidden="true"></g>
    </svg>
    <div class="dpfig__ax" aria-hidden="true"><span style="left:3.57%">990</span><span style="left:26.8%">995</span><span class="n" style="left:50%">N = 1,000</span><span style="left:73.2%">1,005</span><span style="left:96.43%">1,010</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="dpfig__read" aria-hidden="true">
    <span><i>ε</i> = <b data-eps-out>∞</b></span>
    <span>b = 1/<i>ε</i> = <b data-dp="b">0</b></span>
    <span>e<sup><i>ε</i></sup> = <b data-dp="ratio">∞</b></span>
  </div>
  <p class="dpfig__draws"><span class="lab">five releases</span> <span data-dp="draws">1,000 · 1,000 · 1,000 · 1,000 · 1,000</span></p>
  <p class="visually-hidden" aria-live="polite" data-dp="live"></p>
  <figcaption id="fig-laplace-cap"><span class="pl">Fig. 1</span>Releasing a count of N = 1,000 as N + Lap(1/ε). The solid curve is where the release lands for the real data; the dashed one, for the same data with one more person. However the curves move, one is never more than e<sup>ε</sup> times the other: that ratio is the guarantee.</figcaption>
</figure>
<aside class="note note--eps always" id="n-fig-laplace" data-anchor="fig-laplace" data-top="0" aria-label="Privacy budget for Figure 1"><div class="note__in">
  <div class="eps-slot" data-eps-instrument data-hint="The same ε as the portrait on the home page. Lower it and Figure 1 spreads; the text stays as written."></div>
</div></aside>
